1 | devops | Branch feat/floor-terminal from origin/main after the Floor v3 branches have merged (if feat/floor-v3b is not on main yet, branch from origin/feat/floor-v3b and say so in the PR body). Add scripts/floor_tty.py and a make floor target: reads the same live.json the page reads (never the streams directly), renders in the order of docs/proposals/floor-v3-purpose.md section 4 as plain text within 60 lines and 100 columns: the status line first (running, up next, landed, failed, needs you, last event age; stale or offline stated in words before any number), then NEEDS YOU (one line per item with its action and the PR or comment reference as text), NOW grouped by repo (one line per seat: repo, role, issue, task line, status sentence, elapsed), UP NEXT (position, repo, issue, purpose, blocked reason in place), LANDED and FAILED today (failed first). Refreshes every 5 seconds in place, q quits, --once prints and exits for scripting, no colour dependence (one plain and one colour mode, colour only as an addition). Every honesty rule of section 6 holds: queued never shows as running, stale and offline mark every section, replay carries its watermark, no prompt, path or secret appears. Tests: the fixtures the page tests use render to the expected text, width never exceeds 100 columns, stale fixture puts the stale sentence first, --once exits 0. Document it in the README next to make desk-live. VERIFY: the test suite passes with real exit codes in the PR body and a pasted --once render of the live file. HOUSE STYLE: no long dash anywhere, no AI tool or vendor name, no Co-Authored-By trailer. Open a draft PR titled Floor in the terminal, Refs 72. | feat/floor-terminal

2 | plan-critic | READ-ONLY REVIEW of the PR on branch feat/floor-terminal. No commits, no push, no review, no labels; tmp writes only. Record head SHA at start and at report. THE QUESTION THAT MATTERS: can the terminal view ever disagree with the page. Render the same fixtures through both renderers and compare the five answers; then attack the honesty rules (queued as running, stale as live, replay without watermark, a path or prompt in the output), the width at 100 columns with long task lines, and the refresh loop under a missing or malformed live.json (must say so, never crash, never show stale numbers as live). Post ONE comment on the PR whose first line reads CRITIC FLOOR TERMINAL with SAFE-TO-MERGE or BLOCK-FIX and citations. HOUSE STYLE: no long dash, no AI tool or vendor name. | feat/floor-terminal
